<title>USA: US to donate 3,000 tonnes soymeal to Georgia.</title>
<headline>US to donate 3,000 tonnes soymeal to Georgia.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S Agriculture Department said Tuesday that it will donate 3,000 tonnes of soymeal to the former Soviet republic of Georgia.</p>
<p>USDA is making the donation under its fiscal 1997 (October-September) Food for Progres program.</p>
<p>The soymeal will be sold in a sealed bid auction in Georgia to raise funds to support rural credit and agricultural education initiatives there, USDA said.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk 202 898 8341))</p>
</text>
